WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- All right y'all,
(audience applauds)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.340
it's almost time to say goodbye,

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.560
but do not worry, we have
one more story to share.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.690
This is, "#What I'm Liking."

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:07.244
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.244 --> 00:00:09.579
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:00:09.579 --> 00:00:11.573
So I love getting to know the music scene

00:00:11.573 --> 00:00:12.720
here in New York.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.430
This city has always been a magnet

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.260
for up-and-coming performers.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.510
An artist collective
known as Keepsake House

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.040
continues that tradition.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.010
Each live show mixes
songwriting with storytelling,

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.430
creating a Keepsake experience
for the audience, super cool.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:27.690
Let's get the founders in here.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.945
Everybody say hello to Hailey and Jasmine.

00:00:29.945 --> 00:00:32.643
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:00:32.643 --> 00:00:34.550
- What's up y'all?
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.030
- So Hailey, I'm gonna start with you.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.377
You came up with the idea, right?

00:00:37.377 --> 00:00:39.360
- Yeah, both of us did.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.980
So I'm an event planner

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.440
and Jasmine's a musician from New York

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.610
and we sort of saw this need
to have a more community space

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.410
for independent artists here,

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:53.431
especially BIPOC and LGBTQ plus artists

00:00:53.431 --> 00:00:56.691
because it's so competitive in the city.

00:00:56.691 --> 00:00:58.415
So we started Keepsake House,

00:00:58.415 --> 00:01:01.620
which is a home for independent
artists to share the stage

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.990
and make music with meaning.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.940
All of our shows bring together

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.040
songwriters and storytellers.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.490
They share the stage and
learn from each other

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.760
and they also benefit other
like-minded organizations.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.280
So we've actually raised over $7,000

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.410
for Asian Pacific American

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.970
mental health focused organizations.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.507
- Wow, that's so cool.
(audience applauding)

00:01:23.507 --> 00:01:24.660
- Thank you, and yeah,

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.900
ultimately we just wanna
be a home that feels safe

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.660
and supportive for
anyone who comes into it,

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.730
whether a performer or an audience.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.320
- Absolutely, this is, look,

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.210
I lived in Nashville for
like nearly 15 years.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.400
This reminds me of like
walking into like Bluebird

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.233
or a place like that,

00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:40.297
like they have them everywhere there

00:01:40.297 --> 00:01:43.560
and you see these stories,
these songs being told,

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.730
these artists with the songwriters.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:45.630
It's a very cool experience.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.820
Did y'all kind of take a
page from that, Jasmine?

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.940
- Yeah, Hailey and I both
have visited Nashville

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.980
and love that that city,

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.410
and one of the things
we love most about it

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:58.080
is the round table style
shows that they have there

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.180
with multiple artists on stage,

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.340
taking turns playing their songs.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:05.730
We love sort of the openness
and collaboration behind that

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:07.860
and wanted to bring that to New York.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.710
And actually Kelly, we
livestream all of our shows

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:14.319
and we have one coming
up on Friday this week.

00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:15.152
- [Kelly] Yeah?

00:02:15.152 --> 00:02:18.300
- At pinkFROG in Williamsburg, New York,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.500
but you can watch it anywhere.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.660
So if you are around,
we'd love to see you.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:22.830
- Oh, that's incredible.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:24.540
And I can, I just say it's so cool too,

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.700
like you're seeing something different

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.110
every time y'all do these shows.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:30.030
Like these are different
songwriters, different stories,

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.260
different just moments.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.520
I think that's so special, you know?

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.350
Like you're not seeing the
same thing all the time.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:36.030
Like you know, sometimes when
you go on tour to see artists

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.110
that's what you get, you know?

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:38.220
And I think it's really cool

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.750
that you're like specializing
it for the audience.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.400
It's very cool.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.450
- Yeah.
- Thank you.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.307
- We always say you'll never
see another show like it,

00:02:44.307 --> 00:02:47.430
'cause there you won't
see that set of artists

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.083
on stage together.
- Which is cool.

00:02:49.083 --> 00:02:51.450
Like in a time where
everything is always online

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.283
right after it's done,

00:02:52.283 --> 00:02:54.600
it's hard to create
that kind of experience.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.940
So well done and such
a good cause as well.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.795
Thank you so much
Jasmine. Thank you Hailey.

00:02:58.795 --> 00:02:59.628
(audience applauding)

00:02:59.628 --> 00:03:01.650
I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.690
And that's not all, our
season long partner,

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.130
Pilot Pen, makers of FriXion,

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.020
the Go-To Erasable Pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.270
wanna celebrate creators
just like yourselves,

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.130
so they're giving you a thousand dollars,

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.720
that's $500 each
(audience applauding)

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.195
just to help out in whatever way it can.

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:17.276
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much

00:03:17.276 --> 00:03:18.930
and thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:23.131
Brie Larson, Brandy Clark,
Alan Stewart, David Ehrenberg,

00:03:23.131 --> 00:03:24.292
Cash Warren, and Daniel Parnas.

00:03:24.292 --> 00:03:27.660
Y'all have a great day and if
it's not, try and change it.

